The review has been written to `docs/reviews/weather/weather-04-epw-midpoint-offset.md`.

**Summary of findings:**

| # | Severity | Description |
|---|----------|-------------|
| 1 | Medium | HOLIDAYS/DAYLIGHT SAVINGS header discarded, losing `WFAllowsLeapYears` flag — HARES can't detect EPW files that explicitly disallow leap year observation |
| 2 | Medium | PCHIP/cyclic vs linear interpolation difference from EnergyPlus — mathematically correct but not bit-identical; documented divergence in solar (ZOH vs midpoint-triangular) |
| 3 | Low | Hardcoded `hour - 0.5` in `interpolate_ground_temp_c` is redundant with `midpoint_offset_secs` metadata |
| 4 | Low | Leap year auto-detect by record count is correct, preserves Feb 29 (unlike OCHRE which strips it) |
| 5 | Low | Hour field validation (1..=24) matches EPW spec and EnergyPlus |

The 30-minute offset for EPW is confirmed correct for all EPW variants (TMY2, TMY3, AMY, future climate) and does not interact with DST (EPW is always local standard time) or leap years (Feb 29 uses the same hour-ending convention).
